A comforting baked pasta featuring penne enrobed in slow-simmered sausage marinara, layered with creamy ricotta and gooey melted mozzarella.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a29777181/classic-mostaccioli-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

- 2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil
- 1 lb. sweet Italian sausage, removed from casings
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- ⅛ teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes
- 1 can (28 oz) whole peeled tomatoes, pulsed in a blender until smooth
- 1 sprig fresh basil, plus extra chopped for garnish
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 8 oz. penne or mostaccioli pasta
- 1 large egg
- 1 cup whole-milk ricotta cheese
- ½ cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese, divided
- 1 ½ cups shredded mozzarella cheese, divided

## Instructions

1. **Cook the Meat Sauce:** In a deep saucepan over medium heat, warm the olive oil and brown the bulk sausage, breaking it down into bite-sized bits for 8 minutes. Stir in the minced garlic and chili flakes, sautéing for 30 seconds until fragrant. Pour in the pureed canned tomatoes and tuck the whole fresh basil sprig into the sauce. Bring to a boil, then adjust heat to medium-low and simmer uncovered for 15 minutes to reduce slightly. Season with salt and black pepper; pluck out and discard the cooked basil sprig.
2. **Boil the Noodles:** Heat the oven to 450°F (230°C). Bring a generously salted pot of water to a boil and cook the penne or mostaccioli for about 2 minutes less than the carton recommends so it stays firm. Drain in a colander.
3. **Whisk the Ricotta Blend:** In a mixing bowl, beat the egg lightly, then fold in the ricotta cheese, ¼ cup grated Parmesan, and ½ cup shredded mozzarella. Season with a pinch of salt and pepper.
4. **Assemble the Casserole:** Ladle a thin layer of the warm tomato-meat sauce across the base of a 2-quart baking casserole. Scatter the cooked pasta evenly over the bottom layer. Drop spoonfuls of the ricotta mixture over the penne, then coat with the remaining meat sauce. Top the casserole with the remaining ¼ cup Parmesan and the final cup of mozzarella.
5. **Bake High and Hot:** Bake uncovered at 450°F for roughly 15 minutes. The high oven temperature quickly bubbles the sauce and browns the cheese layer without overcooking the pasta. Garnish with chopped fresh basil leaves and rest 5 minutes before scooping.

## Notes

- **Pasta Shapes:** Mostaccioli (smooth tubular pasta) and penne rigate (ridged penne) are interchangeable here.
- **High Heat Finish:** Baking at 450°F gives a quick, bubbly melt and blistered golden cheese crust without drying out the noodles.
